#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cupertino-menud: the cupertino-xfce background helper.

1. Gives every window a Mac-style menu bar (below).
2. When a monitor is plugged in or out, puts the wallpaper and a menu bar on every
   screen (runs `cupertino-xfce-mode monitors`).
3. A wallpaper picked in Desktop Settings goes on every screen and workspace (Xfce
   only changes the screen the settings window is on).

Apps that export their own menus (GTK menubars, Qt, Electron, ...) keep them.
Windows that export nothing, or an empty menu (Firefox, terminals without a
menubar, the desktop itself), get a standard File / Edit / View / Window / Help
set through the AppMenu registrar. Each item sends the app's usual keyboard
shortcut, or runs a small command, so it works with any app.
"""
import os
